PMAT-540 — the PR and its commits name one ticket
=================================================

### 1. the two parsers on the commit the rule exists for
b4719737 is PR #532's merge commit. Its message ENDS like this:
    | Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    | 
    | ---------
    | 
    | Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
  GitHub appends that `---------` + Co-authored-by paragraph itself, and it
  becomes the last paragraph -- the only place git looks for trailers:
  git's %(trailers), whole:                       Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

  git's own %(trailers:key=Pmat-Ticket,valueonly): (nothing)
  read by the LINE:                              PMAT-531 
  pmat's CB-2113 asks git the same way -- src/services/commit_traceability/mod.rs:275
  -- so an arm built on git's parser would be blind to the exact commit
  it exists for.

