  M1 = compare raw ids, never resolving alias:<id>
  M2 = drop the "only when the commits claim SOMETHING" guard
  M3 = make the match arm unreachable, refusing every PR
  M4 = read the trailers with git's own parser instead of the line

  Nine cases, nine killers. The four that survive REMOVAL are over-refusal
  guards by construction -- they assert the arm does not fire -- and each is
  killed by a mutation that makes it fire wrongly.

### 7. what this branch would have paid, under PMAT-542's selection
  the whole diff:            code=true gate_c=true gate_d=true gates=C,D 
  the diff without .github/: code=true gate_c=false gate_d=false gates=none 
  The one .github/ line is this suite being added to the guard job's list. Gate
  C and gate D read nothing else this branch touches, so without it the branch
  would be the first `gates=none` PR since PMAT-542 landed -- 21.3 of 25.2
  critical-path minutes, not paid.

  It is paid on purpose. The integration suites DO run in CI under the coverage
  job (`cargo llvm-cov` builds and runs every test binary), so naming this one
  in the guard list buys ORDERING -- a fast red before the slow jobs -- rather
  than coverage. Its sibling falsification_dogfood_harness_and_quorum is already
  in that list.

